# Git & issues (OpenCAD)

## Branches

- **Never** commit or push directly to `main` or `develop`.
- `main` = releases only, via PR **from `develop`**.
- `develop` = integration only, via PR **from `feature/*` or `fix/*`**.
- Work only on `feature/<kebab-title>` or `fix/<kebab-title>`, branched from `develop`.

## Commits

- Every commit **must** reference an issue (`(#123)` / `Fixes #123`).
- Every commit has a **subject + body** (message and description).
- Commits are **atomic** (one coherent, revertable change).
- Prefer: `type: summary (#N)` then blank line then description.

## Issues

- Issues must state explicit **DOR** (Definition of Ready) and **DOD** (Definition of Done).
- Do not start work on an issue missing DOR/DOD — add them first.
- Canonical doc: `documentation/contribution-rules.md`
